Did you check with scope if there is data being transmitted?

You don’t check the HAL status so how do you know if it was a good send?

```

HAL_StatusTypeDef hal_status = HAL_OK;

hal_status = HAL_UART_Transmit_DMA(...);

if(hal_status != HAL_OK)

{

// do something

}

```

From there you can check what hal\_status returns, HAL\_OK, HAL\_BUSY or HAL\_ERROR

For a quick check, just use HAL\_UART\_Transmit to see if it’s a HW or UART configuration setup issue.
